ume  many more go unnoticed just having a  data leak can cause a company to lose  contracts especially if clients don't  feel confidential information is safe  these companies involve lots of  innovation with a great deal of  knowledge about production methods and  processes in a highly industrialized  world if the differences between  technologies are no longer that large so  information is key who are the best  subcontractors and lucrative clients and  what are the margins that's the data  attackers are trying to get no one knows  exactly how many cyber attacks on German  companies are successful but the  Federation of German industry assumes  the country's businesses are attractive  targets for industrial ackers all over  the world it's hard for us to estimate  the damage done to German industry  through industrial espionage and cyber  security issues but the Interior  Ministry believes it costs between 20  and 50 billion euros annually unreported  damages could drive that number way up  but the startup entrepreneurs in Berlin  don't just rely on strong encryption  when their data was stolen only good  relations with clients helped them  through the crisis now they've made  personal interaction with customers a  cornerstone of their business strategy
 

